{=============================================================================
  Free convection from cylinders: Nusselt-number correlations for vertical and
  horizontal cylinders
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0092 (function library, kind = function)
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Ten correlations for natural convection from a vertical cylinder (Griffiths,
  Davis & Morgan 1922; Jakob & Linke 1935; Carne 1937; Eigenson 1940;
  Touloukian, Hawkins & Jakob 1948; Weise 1935 / Saunders 1936 / McAdams;
  Eckert & Jackson 1950 / Kreith, Manglik & Bohn; Hanesian & Kalish 1970;
  Al-Arabi & Khamis 1982; Popiel, Wojtkowiak & Bober 2007) and three for a
  horizontal cylinder (Churchill & Chu 1975; Kuehn & Goldstein 1976; Morgan
  1975), all in the presentation of Morgan, V.T., "The Overall Convective Heat
  Transfer from Smooth Circular Cylinders", Advances in Heat Transfer 11,
  199-264 (1975).

  All of them return the Nusselt number of the cylinder; the surface
  heat-transfer coefficient follows from h = Nu*k/D and is left to the caller.
  The fluid properties enter only through the dimensionless groups Pr and Gr
  (Ra = Pr*Gr), which are arguments: no property function is called inside a
  function, so the calling model passes Pr and Gr itself.

  Eight of the ten vertical-cylinder correlations are piecewise in Ra (laminar
  and turbulent branches joined without smoothing) and therefore take the
  argument `turbulent`: -1 selects the branch automatically from Ra (the ht
  default, None), 0 forces the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent branch.

  The demonstration program at the end calls every function once with the input
  set of the ht doctest of the corresponding correlation ("A" cases), once
  with both branches forced ("A_lam", "A_turb") and once with a second uniform
  input set ("B" cases). The ht values of all the sets are tabulated in the
  README (verification table).

  Two selectors of the ht family are only dispatchers
  (Nu_vertical_cylinder(_methods), Nu_horizontal_cylinder(_methods): they select
  a method by name) and are not translated; an EES caller selects the function
  directly.

  Inputs : Pr [-], Gr [-] (on the cylinder height, vertical; on the cylinder
           diameter, horizontal), L [m], D [m], turbulent [-]
  Outputs: Nu [-] (one FUNCTION per correlation)
  Units  : SI - dimensionless numbers, lengths in m
  Source : ht (Caleb Bell), ht/conv_free_immersed.py, version 1.2.0, commit
           85e0ee6, MIT - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht ; correlations by the
           authors cited in each function block - see README.md
  Status : VERIFIED against the doctests and the values of ht 1.2.0
           (README.md, "Verification")
=============================================================================}

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_GRIFFITHS_DAVIS_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection
from a vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Griffiths, Davis & Great Britain
(1922) correlated by Morgan (1975).

  Nu_H = 0.67*Ra_H^0.25      1E7 < Ra < 1E9
  Nu_H = 0.0782*Ra_H^0.357   1E9 < Ra < 1E11,   Ra = Pr*Gr

turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent one. The transition between the two
ranges is not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Data: cylinder of diameter 17.43 cm, length from 4.65 to 263.5 cm, air.
Validity: the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Griffiths, E., A. H. Davis and Great Britain, "The Transmission of
  Heat by Radiation and Convection", London: H. M. Stationery Office, 1922;
  correlated by Morgan, V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat Transfer from Smooth
  Circular Cylinders", in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and
  J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264, 1975; as presented in Popiel, C. O., "Free
  Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A Review", Heat
  Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008, and in Boetcher, S. K. S.,
  "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural
  Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 1E9 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan = 0.0782*Ra^0.357
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan = 0.67*Ra^0.25
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_JAKOB_LINKE_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection
from a vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Jakob & Linke (1935)
correlated by Morgan (1975).

  Nu_H = 0.555*Ra_H^0.25   1E4 < Ra < 1E8
  Nu_H = 0.129*Ra_H^(1/3)  1E8 < Ra < 1E12,   Ra = Pr*Gr

turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent one. The transition between the two
ranges is not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Data: cylinder of diameter 3.5 cm, length from L/D = 4.3, air.
Validity: the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Jakob, M. and W. Linke, "Warmeubergang beim Verdampfen von
  Flussigkeiten an senkrechten und waagerechten Flaschen", Phys. Z., 36,
  267-280, 1935; correlated by Morgan, V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat
  Transfer from Smooth Circular Cylinders", in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds.
  T. F. Irvin and J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264, 1975; as presented in Popiel,
  C. O., "Free Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A
  Review", Heat Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008, and in
  Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical
  Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer,
  2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 1E8 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan = 0.129*Ra^(1/3)
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan = 0.555*Ra^0.25
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_CARNE_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection from a
vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Carne (1937) correlated by
Morgan (1975).

  Nu_H = 1.07*Ra_H^0.28    2E6 < Ra < 2E8
  Nu_H = 0.152*Ra_H^0.38   2E8 < Ra < 2E11,   Ra = Pr*Gr

turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent one. The transition between the two
ranges is not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Data: cylinder of diameters 0.475 cm to 7.62 cm, L/D from 8 to 127; the
isothermal boundary condition was assumed but not verified.
Validity: the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Carne, J. B., "LIX. Heat Loss by Natural Convection from Vertical
  Cylinders", The London, Edinburgh, and Dublin Philosophical Magazine and
  Journal of Science 24(162): 634-653, 1 October 1937; correlated by Morgan,
  V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat Transfer from Smooth Circular Cylinders",
  in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and J. P. Hartnett, 11,
  199-264, 1975; as presented in Popiel, C. O., "Free Convection Heat Transfer
  from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A Review", Heat Transfer Engineering 29(6):
  521-536, 1 June 2008, and in Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat
  Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular
  Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 2E8 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan = 0.152*Ra^0.38
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan = 1.07*Ra^0.28
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_EIGENSON_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection from
a vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Eigenson (1940) correlated by
Morgan (1975); the only correlation of the family with three branches, the
middle one being the transition formula.

  Nu_H = 0.48*Ra_H^0.25                  Ra <= 1E9
  Nu_H = 51.5 + 0.0000726*Ra_H^0.63      1E9 < Ra < 1.69E10
  Nu_H = 0.148*Ra_H^(1/3) - 127.6        Ra > 1.69E10,   Ra = Pr*Gr

sel = 0, 1 and 2 select the first, second and third form; the ht docstring
prints the range of the first form as 10^9 < Ra, which its code contradicts.
turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the first (lowest-Rayleigh) form, 1 forces the third one. The transitions are
not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Data: height 2.5 m with diameters of 2.4, 7.55, 15, 35 and 50 mm, another
experiment with a diameter of 58 mm and a length of 6.5 m; results presented as
appropriate for both flat plates and cylinders.
Validity: the three Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Eigenson, L., "Les lois gouvernant la transmission de la chaleur aux
  gaz biatomiques par les parois des cylindres verticaux dans le cas de
  convection naturelle", Dokl. Akad. Nauk SSSR 26: 440-444, 1940; correlated by
  Morgan, V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat Transfer from Smooth Circular
  Cylinders", in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and J. P. Hartnett,
  11, 199-264, 1975; as presented in Popiel, C. O., "Free Convection Heat
  Transfer from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A Review", Heat Transfer
  Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008, and in more detail in Boetcher,
  S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in
  Natural Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014 (only this
  one shows the transition formula).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 2
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 1.69E10 THEN
        sel = 2
      ELSE
        IF Ra > 1E9 THEN
          sel = 1
        ELSE
          sel = 0
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 2 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan = 0.148*Ra^(1/3) - 127.6
  ELSE
    IF sel = 1 THEN
      Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan = 51.5 + 0.0000726*Ra^0.63
    ELSE
      Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan = 0.48*Ra^0.25
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_TOULOUKIAN_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection from
a vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Touloukian, Hawkins & Jakob (1948)
correlated by Morgan (1975).

  Nu_H = 0.726*Ra_H^0.25                 2E8 < Ra < 4E10
  Nu_H = 0.0674*(Gr_H*Pr^1.29)^(1/3)      4E10 < Ra < 9E11,   Ra = Pr*Gr

Note that the turbulent branch is written with Gr and Pr, not with Ra, as in
the original.
turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent one. The transition between the two
ranges is not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Data: cylinder of diameter 2.75 inch with heights of 6, 18 and 36.25 inch,
temperature controlled by separately controlled heating sections; fluids water
and ethylene-glycol.
Validity: the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Touloukian, Y. S., G. A. Hawkins and M. Jakob, "Heat Transfer by
  Free Convection from Heated Vertical Surfaces to Liquids", Trans. ASME 70,
  13-18, 1948; correlated by Morgan, V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat
  Transfer from Smooth Circular Cylinders", in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds.
  T. F. Irvin and J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264, 1975; as presented in Popiel,
  C. O., "Free Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A
  Review", Heat Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008, and in
  Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical
  Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer,
  2014 (all three in complete agreement on this formulation).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 4E10 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan = 0.0674*(Gr*Pr^1.29)^(1/3)
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan = 0.726*Ra^0.25
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_MCADAMS_WEISS_SAUNDERS - Nusselt number, natural convection
from a vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Weise (1935) and Saunders
(1936) correlated by Morgan (1975).

  Nu_H = 0.59*Ra_H^0.25   1E4 < Ra < 1E9
  Nu_H = 0.13*Ra_H^(1/3)   1E9 < Ra < 1E12,   Ra = Pr*Gr

turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent one. The transition between the two
ranges is not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given; for
Ra below 1E4 the original gives a graph, not reproduced here.
Validity: the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Weise, R., "Warmeubergang durch freie Konvektion an quadratischen
  Platten", Forschung auf dem Gebiet des Ingenieurwesens A 6(6): 281-292,
  November 1935, and Saunders, O. A., "The Effect of Pressure Upon Natural
  Convection in Air", Proceedings of the Royal Society of London A: Mathematical,
  Physical and Engineering Sciences 157(891): 278-291, 2 November 1936,
  correlated by Morgan, V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat Transfer from
  Smooth Circular Cylinders", in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and
  J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264, 1975, and in McAdams, W. H., Heat Transmission,
  3E, Malabar, Fla: Krieger Pub Co, 1985; as presented in Popiel, C. O., "Free
  Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A Review", Heat
  Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008, and in Boetcher, S. K. S.,
  "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural
  Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 1E9 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders = 0.13*Ra^(1/3)
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders = 0.59*Ra^0.25
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert(Pr, Gr, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_KREITH_ECKERT - Nusselt number, natural convection from a
vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Eckert & Jackson (1950) correlated by
Kreith, Manglik & Bohn.

  Nu_H = 0.555*Ra_H^0.25   1E5 < Ra < 1E9
  Nu_H = 0.021*Ra_H^0.4    1E9 < Ra < 1E12,   Ra = Pr*Gr

turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the laminar branch, 1 forces the turbulent one. The transition between the two
ranges is not smooth (as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Validity: the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Eckert, E. R. G. and T. W. Jackson, "Analysis of Turbulent
  Free-Convection Boundary Layer on Flat Plate", National Advisory Committee for
  Aeronautics 2207, Washington, D.C.: National Advisory Committee for
  Aeronautics, 1950, correlated by Kreith, F., R. Manglik and M. Bohn,
  Principles of Heat Transfer, Cengage, 2010; as presented in Morgan, V. T.,
  "The Overall Convective Heat Transfer from Smooth Circular Cylinders", in
  Advances in Heat Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264,
  1975, in Popiel, C. O., "Free Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical Slender
  Cylinders: A Review", Heat Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008,
  and in Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical
  Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer,
  2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 1E9 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert = 0.021*Ra^0.4
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert = 0.555*Ra^0.25
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan(Pr, Gr)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_HANESIAN_KALISH_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection
from a vertical isothermal cylinder, results of Hanesian & Kalish (1970)
correlated by Morgan (1975); laminar range only, so the function has no regime
argument.

  Nu_H = 0.48*Ra_H^0.23    1E6 < Ra < 1E8,   Ra = Pr*Gr

Outside the range, no warning is given.
Data: air and fluorocarbon gases.
Validity: 1E6 < Ra < 1E8.
Original: Hanesian, D. and R. Kalish, "Heat Transfer by Natural Convection
  with Fluorocarbon Gases", IEEE Transactions on Parts, Materials and Packaging
  6(4): 147-148, December 1970; correlated by Morgan, V. T., "The Overall
  Convective Heat Transfer from Smooth Circular Cylinders", in Advances in Heat
  Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264, 1975; as
  presented in Popiel, C. O., "Free Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical
  Slender Cylinders: A Review", Heat Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536,
  1 June 2008, and in Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat Transfer
  From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular Cylinders,
  23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan = 0.48*Ra^0.23
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis(Pr, Gr, L, D, turbulent)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_AL_ARABI_KHAMIS - Nusselt number, natural convection from
a vertical isothermal cylinder (air), Al-Arabi & Khamis.

  Nu_H = 2.9*Ra_H^0.25/Gr_D^(1/12)     9.88E7 <= Ra <= 2.7E9
  Nu_H = 0.47*Ra_H^(1/3)/Gr_D^(1/12)   2.7E9 <= Ra <= 2.95E10
  Gr_D = Gr*(D/L)^3,   Ra = Pr*Gr,   Gr is taken on the cylinder height [m]

The switch between the two forms is at Ra = 2.6E9 in the ht code and at
2.7E9 in its docstring; the function follows the code, as the ranges of the two
forms overlap. Outside the range, no warning is given.
turbulent = -1 selects the branch from Ra (automatic, the ht default), 0 forces
the first (lower-Rayleigh) form, 1 forces the second one.
Data: D from 12.75 to 51 mm, height from 300 to 2000 mm; the temperature kept
constant by steam condensing.
Validity: 1.08E4 <= Gr_D <= 6.9E5 and the two Rayleigh-number ranges above.
Original: Al-Arabi, M. and M. Khamis, "Natural Convection Heat Transfer from
  Inclined Cylinders", International Journal of Heat and Mass Transfer 25(1):
  3-15, January 1982; as presented in Popiel, C. O., "Free Convection Heat
  Transfer from Vertical Slender Cylinders: A Review", Heat Transfer
  Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008, and in Boetcher, S. K. S.,
  "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural
  Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Gr_D = Gr*(D/L)^3
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF turbulent = 1 THEN
    sel = 1
  ELSE
    IF turbulent = 0 THEN
      sel = 0
    ELSE
      IF Ra > 2.6E9 THEN
        sel = 1
      ELSE
        sel = 0
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IF sel = 1 THEN
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis = 0.47*Ra^(1/3)*Gr_D^(-1/12)
  ELSE
    Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis = 2.9*Ra^0.25*Gr_D^(-1/12)
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill(Pr, Gr, L, D)
{NU_VERTICAL_CYLINDER_POPIEL_CHURCHILL - Nusselt number, natural convection from
a vertical isothermal cylinder, as a correction of the vertical flat-plate
Nusselt number (laminar; the correlation has no regime argument).

  Nu      = Nu_fp*{1 + B*[32^0.5*Gr_L^(-0.25)*(L/D)]^C}
  B       = 0.0571322 + 0.20305*Pr^(-0.43)
  C       = 0.9165 - 0.0043*Pr^0.5 + 0.01333*LN(Pr) + 0.0004809/Pr
  Nu_fp   = [0.825 + 0.387*Ra_L^(1/6)/{1+(0.492/Pr)^(9/16)}^(8/27)]^2

Gr is taken on the cylinder height L [m] and Ra = Pr*Gr; L and D are the
cylinder height and diameter [m]. Nu_fp is the Churchill-Chu correlation for a
vertical plate, which ht computes internally by calling its
Nu_vertical_plate_Churchill (see the reference below; it is a member of another
family of the same module, HT-007); its equations are repeated here so that this
function is self-contained.
Validity: 0.01 < Pr < 100 (as in ht). Popiel's review and Boetcher's chapter
print a power of 2 instead of 0.5 on the 32 of the equation; the original has
the correct form, which is the one used here.
Original: Popiel, C. O., J. Wojtkowiak and K. Bober, "Laminar Free Convective
  Heat Transfer from Isothermal Vertical Slender Cylinder", Experimental
  Thermal and Fluid Science 32(2): 607-613, November 2007; as presented in
  Popiel, C. O., "Free Convection Heat Transfer from Vertical Slender
  Cylinders: A Review", Heat Transfer Engineering 29(6): 521-536, 1 June 2008,
  and in Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical
  Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer,
  2014.
  Nu_fp as in Churchill, S. W. and H. H. S. Chu, "Correlating Equations for
  Laminar and Turbulent Free Convection from a Vertical Plate", International
  Journal of Heat and Mass Transfer 18(11): 1323-1329, 1 November 1975, and in
  Bergman, T. L., A. S. Lavine, F. P. Incropera and D. P. DeWitt, Introduction
  to Heat Transfer, 6E, Hoboken, NJ: Wiley, 2011.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill (with Nu_vertical_plate_Churchill),
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  Nu_fp = (0.825 + 0.387*Ra^(1/6)/(1 + (0.492/Pr)^(9/16))^(8/27))^2
  B = 0.0571322 + 0.20305*Pr^(-0.43)
  C = 0.9165 - 0.0043*Pr^0.5 + 0.01333*LN(Pr) + 0.0004809/Pr
  Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill = Nu_fp*(1 + B*(32^0.5*Gr^(-0.25)*L/D)^C)
END

FUNCTION Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu(Pr, Gr)
{NU_HORIZONTAL_CYLINDER_CHURCHILL_CHU - Nusselt number, natural convection from
a horizontal isothermal cylinder, Churchill & Chu (1975); the equation gives a
smooth transition from the laminar to the turbulent regime.

  Nu_D = [0.60 + 0.387*Ra_D^(1/6)/{1+(0.559/Pr)^(9/16)}^(8/27)]^2
  Ra = Pr*Gr,  Gr is taken on the cylinder diameter

Checked with the original source, whose powers are unsimplified but equivalent.
Validity: 1E-5 as lower limit of Ra with no upper limit in the original;
Incropera et al. suggest an upper limit of 1E12. Outside the range, no warning
is given.
Original: Churchill, S. W. and H. H. S. Chu, "Correlating Equations for Laminar
  and Turbulent Free Convection from a Horizontal Cylinder", International
  Journal of Heat and Mass Transfer 18(9): 1049-1053, September 1975; as
  presented in Bergman, T. L., A. S. Lavine, F. P. Incropera and D. P. DeWitt,
  Introduction to Heat Transfer, 6E, Hoboken, NJ: Wiley, 2011.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu = (0.6 + 0.387*Ra^(1/6)/(1 + (0.559/Pr)^(9/16))^(8/27))^2
END

FUNCTION Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein(Pr, Gr)
{NU_HORIZONTAL_CYLINDER_KUEHN_GOLDSTEIN - Nusselt number, natural convection from
a horizontal isothermal cylinder, Kuehn & Goldstein (1976).

  2/Nu_D = LN[1 + 2/{[{0.518*Ra_D^0.25*[1+(0.559/Pr)^0.6]^(-5/12)}^15
                          + (0.1*Ra_D^(1/3))^15]^(1/15)}]
  Ra = Pr*Gr,  Gr is taken on the cylinder diameter

Validity: the original suggests this expression is valid in all cases except
for low-Prandtl-number fluids; Incropera et al. suggest no restriction
(as in ht). Outside the range, no warning is given.
Original: Kuehn, T. H. and R. J. Goldstein, "Correlating Equations for Natural
  Convection Heat Transfer between Horizontal Circular Cylinders",
  International Journal of Heat and Mass Transfer 19(10): 1127-1134,
  October 1976; as presented in Boetcher, S. K. S., "Natural Convection Heat
  Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural Convection from Circular
  Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein = 2/LN(1 + 2/((0.518*Ra^0.25*(1 + (0.559/Pr)^0.6)^(-5/12))^15 + (0.1*Ra^(1/3))^15)^(1/15))
END

FUNCTION Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan(Pr, Gr)
{NU_HORIZONTAL_CYLINDER_MORGAN - Nusselt number, natural convection from a
horizontal isothermal cylinder, Morgan (1975): a power law per Rayleigh-number
range, the most comprehensive review of the literature.

  Nu_D = C*Ra_D^n,   Ra = Pr*Gr,  Gr is taken on the cylinder diameter

  Ra range         C       n
  Ra < 1E-2       0.675    0.058
  1E-2 <= Ra < 1E2  1.020  0.148
  1E2 <= Ra < 1E4  0.850  0.188
  1E4 <= Ra < 1E7  0.480  0.250
  Ra >= 1E7       0.125    0.333  (up to 1E12)

The correlation is discontinuous at the range limits (as in ht); it runs outside
of them without warning.
Original: Morgan, V. T., "The Overall Convective Heat Transfer from Smooth
  Circular Cylinders", in Advances in Heat Transfer, eds. T. F. Irvin and
  J. P. Hartnett, 11, 199-264, 1975; as presented in Boetcher, S. K. S.,
  "Natural Convection Heat Transfer From Vertical Cylinders", in Natural
  Convection from Circular Cylinders, 23-42, Springer, 2014.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_free_immersed.py,
  Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Ra = Pr*Gr
  IF Ra < 1E-2 THEN
    C = 0.675
    n = 0.058
  ELSE
    IF Ra < 1E2 THEN
      C = 1.02
      n = 0.148
    ELSE
      IF Ra < 1E4 THEN
        C = 0.85
        n = 0.188
      ELSE
        IF Ra < 1E7 THEN
          C = 0.48
          n = 0.25
        ELSE
          C = 0.125
          n = 0.333
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan = C*Ra^n
END

"!Demonstration program: every correlation is called at least once"
"It is ignored by the future $INCLUDE library:free_conv_cylinders (CS-FEAT-IMPORT)."
"Case A: the input set of the ht doctest of each correlation (published values)."
"Case A_lam / A_turb: the same inputs with the laminar and the turbulent branch"
"  forced, which exercises both sides of the non-smooth regime switches."
"Case B: one second, uniform input set (Pr = 0.71, Gr = 1E10, L = 1.5 m, D = 0.15 m)."
"All three sets are tabulated against ht in the README (verification table)."

"Case A - input sets (the ht doctests)"
Pr_A_vert = 0.7       "air, ht doctests of the six correlations of case A with Gr = 2E10"
Gr_A_vert = 2E10
Pr_A_Carne = 0.7
Gr_A_Carne = 2E8
Pr_A_Hanesian = 0.7
Gr_A_Hanesian = 1E7
Pr_A_Al_Arabi = 0.71
Gr_A_Al_Arabi = 2E10
L_A_Al_Arabi = 10     "cylinder height [m], as in the ht doctest"
D_A_Al_Arabi = 1      "cylinder diameter [m], as in the ht doctest"
Pr_A_Popiel = 0.7
Gr_A_Popiel = 1E10
L_A_Popiel = 2.5      "cylinder height [m], as in the ht doctest"
D_A_Popiel = 1        "cylinder diameter [m], as in the ht doctest"
Pr_A_horiz = 0.69
Gr_A_horiz = 2.63E9

"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan(Pr_A_Carne, Gr_A_Carne, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan(Pr_A_Hanesian, Gr_A_Hanesian)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis(Pr_A_Al_Arabi, Gr_A_Al_Arabi, L_A_Al_Arabi, D_A_Al_Arabi, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill_A = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill(Pr_A_Popiel, Gr_A_Popiel, L_A_Popiel, D_A_Popiel)
"Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu"
Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu_A = Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu(Pr_A_horiz, Gr_A_horiz)
"Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein"
Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein_A = Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein(Pr_A_horiz, Gr_A_horiz)
"Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan"
Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan_A = Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan(Pr_A_horiz, Gr_A_horiz)

"Case A_lam / A_turb - both branches of the eight regime switches, forced"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan(Pr_A_Carne, Gr_A_Carne, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis_A_lam = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis(Pr_A_Al_Arabi, Gr_A_Al_Arabi, L_A_Al_Arabi, D_A_Al_Arabi, 0)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan(Pr_A_Carne, Gr_A_Carne, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert(Pr_A_vert, Gr_A_vert, 1)
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis_A_turb = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis(Pr_A_Al_Arabi, Gr_A_Al_Arabi, L_A_Al_Arabi, D_A_Al_Arabi, 1)

"Case B - second, uniform input set"
Pr_B = 0.71        "air [-]"
Gr_B = 1E10        "Grashof number [-]"
L_B = 1.5          "cylinder height [m]"
D_B = 0.15         "cylinder diameter [m]"

"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Griffiths_Davis_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Jakob_Linke_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Carne_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Eigenson_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Touloukian_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_McAdams_Weiss_Saunders(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Kreith_Eckert(Pr_B, Gr_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Hanesian_Kalish_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Al_Arabi_Khamis(Pr_B, Gr_B, L_B, D_B, -1)
"Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill"
Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill_B = Nu_vertical_cylinder_Popiel_Churchill(Pr_B, Gr_B, L_B, D_B)
"Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu"
Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu_B = Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Churchill_Chu(Pr_B, Gr_B)
"Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein"
Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein_B = Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Kuehn_Goldstein(Pr_B, Gr_B)
"Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan"
Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan_B = Nu_horizontal_cylinder_Morgan(Pr_B, Gr_B)